ngage really hard with  our partner ecosystem we really want to  enable our partners and help our  partners help our customers get this  data into the system so first one is the  offline ingest so we work with Iron  Mountain in the US for offline ingest  and prime focus in abroad for helping  people do offline ingest  so if you have petabytes of data or even  lots of terabytes of data that you want  to get moved in the system you can put  them into a hard drive and you can ship  those to Iron Mountain and they will  upload those data that data into Google  Cloud storage for you same thing in  outside the United States the other area  that we really invested in since we  invented since we announced Nearline  last year was the filer and the  on-premise file systems so in the middle  of last year we announced the ability of  Nearline so within Google Cloud  storage we now have three different  storage classes the first one is  standard which is what people have been  using to static to host their static web  content and when they're using their  data processing pipelines durable  reduced availability which in exchange  for a slightly lower SLA of availability  you get a price break which is our  second class and then the third one we  introduced last year is near line and  near line is our warm storage archival  solution that allows you to put your  data into a GC GC a GCS bucket with near  line for basically archival and as part  of that we've been working with all of  our partners in the space to help  facilitate that for customers a lot of  these partners have huge cost of huge  enterprise footprints on-premise and  they want to be able to back up their  files to the cloud so how do we enable  that and make it easy for customers to  do that so working with the customers  like NetApp CommVault emc aveer making  sure that when you are running those  appliances on Prem or some of them in a  cloud appliance there is the option for  you to then push that data into Google  Cloud storage so that you can back it up  and again have Google's esterase looking  after your data to make sure that it is  safe and secure and always there when  you need it the last one that I would  like to talk about is data pipeline so  we've talked a little bit about this  earlier so great I've got 500 petabytes  of data in Google Cloud storage now what  it's been sitting on pram I've never  done anything with it like what is the  value to me and most people just want it  as optionality in case of a disaster  right they either need to keep it from a  compliance point of view or they just  want to make sure there's something  happens they have a copy their data  what's so great about this integrated  data platform approach is that once you  get your data into the system we can  provide lots of interesting tools for  you to be able to then take that data  and derive value from it so first one we  talked a little bit about earlier is  data flow so if you want to either do  batch or streaming and we just recently  pushed this into Apache as Apache beam  you can use data flow to run large batch  or stream processes over your 500  petabytes of data to basically clean it  extract value Tran  formant push it into bigquery do  whatever you need to do with it  and again fully managed service if you  need one petabyte of data or 500 pen  types of data it's the same code it's  running the same in the same  infrastructure the same set of api's so  we can scale ibly go through your data  and help you derive value the second one  is data proc and there's another talk  just after this one on data proc which I  encourage you guys to attend so dana  proc is really helping customers that  are running large on Prem Hadoop  installations to be able to easily move  those workloads to the cloud so if you  have a MapReduce job that you've been  running on Prem once you push all that  data into Google Cloud Storage you want  to be able to run that MapReduce so data  proc allows you to just bring that  MapReduce into Google cloud platform and  run that MapReduce over your 500  petabytes of data to get whatever value  or extraction data extracted out of that  information and then many of these if  you're doing that information if you're  doing that processing and trying to  extract the value you often need a place  to put that data so many times people  are running these dataflow jobs and data  probes and pushing data into bigquery  into a data warehouse where they can  then run their distributed queries  another thing that I'm very excited  about the direction we're going which  really speaks to the idea that you can  put your data anywhere and will help you  drive value is within bigquery you can  actually do federated queries so you can  do queries against your data that's  already in bigquery but you can also do  joins in queries against your data in  GCS so if you have your data in an Avro  or Park a file in GCS you can run  bigquery queries against that data and  potentially join it with data that you  have in bigquery but where this becomes  really interesting is that we can then  expand those federico aires out to cloud  BigTable and data store and all these  other areas so that regardless of where  your data is you don't have to ETL it  and move it into another solution and  you don't have to ETL it into and by ETL  is extract transform and load you don't  have to have a process to move that data  into bigquery you can just do the  queries from bigquery and query your  data in line so that's where it starts  to get really compelling where wherever  your data is in the Google cloud  platform  you'll be able to then access that data  and drive value from it without having  to move it around and worry about where  it is one other thing  so in data proc so if you're using a  base we have HBase connectors so you use  that as an intermediate point in data  proc also connectors for data flow so  making sure that all of these various  products